{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0440", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$B \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0003": "$B$", "MATH_0004": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0005": "$(\\mathcal{F}, \\alpha)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{O}_U$", "MATH_0008": "$\\alpha$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{O}_R$", "MATH_0010": "$$\n\\alpha : t^*\\mathcal{F} \\longrightarrow s^*\\mathcal{F}\n$$", "MATH_0011": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n& \\text{pr}_1^*t^*\\mathcal{F} \\ar[r]_-{\\text{pr}_1^*\\alpha} &\n\\text{pr}_1^*s^*\\mathcal{F} \\ar@{=}[rd] & \\\\\n\\text{pr}_0^*s^*\\mathcal{F} \\ar@{=}[ru] & & & c^*s^*\\mathcal{F} \\\\\n& \\text{pr}_0^*t^*\\mathcal{F} \\ar[lu]^{\\text{pr}_0^*\\alpha} \\ar@{=}[r] &\nc^*t^*\\mathcal{F} \\ar[ru]_{c^*\\alpha}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{O}_{R \\times_{s, U, t} R}$", "MATH_0013": "$$\ne^*\\alpha : \\mathcal{F} \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{F}\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-notation}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-diagram}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-groupoid-module}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:39d6570281cfc402c43f76ec90cfd3a2b9f6ef1af904c014d44ed2662908b90c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d591ab54fc422d495a0a43567b11c7d2e839076df265ba5bda11adaf381bb95e", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> as in Section <REF_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a groupoid in algebraic spaces over <MATH_0003>.\nA <TEXTITOPEN_0001>quasi-coherent module on <MATH_0004><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nis a pair <MATH_0005>, where <MATH_0006> is a quasi-coherent\n<MATH_0007>-module, and <MATH_0008> is a <MATH_0009>-module\nmap\n<MATH_0010>\nsuch that\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> the diagram\n<MATH_0011>\nis a commutative in the category of\n<MATH_0012>-modules, and\n<STRUCT_0003> the pullback\n<MATH_0013>\nis the identity map.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nCompare with the commutative diagrams of Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cf801c3c352c24bcf4a9383c50201b5014834d191d3fb3beeb7fc3233811cff9", "unit_id": "tag:0441:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0440", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$e^*\\alpha$", "MATH_0002": "$e^*\\alpha$", "MATH_0003": "$\\alpha$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f93a890da7e9c964cd54b0220589d1cc6fa268c93aac0302c2ab346769a9496b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:29f1cb4a2f348641c0393b6e558518b9b3b536683fc861b04d0e610e2ffa3314", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe commutativity of the first diagram forces the operator <MATH_0001>\nto be idempotent. Hence the second condition can be reformulated as saying\nthat <MATH_0002> is an isomorphism. In fact, the condition implies that\n<MATH_0003> is an isomorphism.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:484008bd8e8d033f2e5ecf0e6feb8b149b8ecb5ee9dac72e6399d6a3257b5c2d", "unit_id": "tag:0440:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0440", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$B \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0003": "$B$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\mathcal{F}, \\alpha)$", "MATH_0005": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\alpha$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-notation}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-isomorphism}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c18590a0ed3b5c583decec337b66de62361190ab2bb2a46a4886b4dbc06cf98f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:48cf500319263b472f0f73ec1e7288bbb665c020da926bdf9735124936748ace", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> as in Section <REF_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a groupoid in algebraic spaces over <MATH_0003>.\nIf <MATH_0004> is a quasi-coherent module on <MATH_0005>\nthen <MATH_0006> is an isomorphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a710eaf4ebc06d940cb481ed870bc461e0fd1c7e3c87c1b115c04fc4f124967e", "unit_id": "tag:077W:statement"}
